# Build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# All user-supplied game data lives here and is NEVER committed.
# `/data/*` rather than `/data/`: git cannot re-include a file from inside an
# excluded directory, so the directory itself must stay traversable.
/data/*
!/data/README.md

# Belt-and-braces: even outside /data/, no game content may ever be committed.
# These patterns exist so a stray copy in the wrong directory still gets caught.
*.chd
*.iso
*.cso
*.pkg
*.pbp
*.umd
*.wad
*.elf
*.prx
*.self
*.BIN
*.bin
*.img
*.gcm

# SMAA's own precomputed lookup textures (AreaTex/SearchTex), MIT-licensed
# third-party shader data - not extracted disc content. See
# scripts/check-leakage.py's ALLOWED_TRACKED, which must stay in sync.
!/crates/render/src/post/smaa_area.bin
!/crates/render/src/post/smaa_search.bin

# Reproductions this project itself writes, not just source content: a
# `--screenshot` is a rendering of the disc's models and textures, and the
# movie cache demuxes to these four formats (crates/game/src/movie.rs). See
# scripts/check-leakage.py, which is the single source of truth this list
# must stay in sync with.
*.png
*.ivf
!/crates/formats/tests/data/testsrc-64x64.ivf
*.h264
*.ipu
*.pss
*.mip
*.vex
*.fnt
*.pmf

# Packaged builds and the packaging tool. `just appimage` writes into
# data/appimage/, which /data/* already covers; this catches an AppImage built
# with --out somewhere else, since no binary is ever committed either.
*.AppImage

# Ghidra. Note: deliberately NOT `*.lock`, which would swallow Cargo.lock.
# This workspace commits Cargo.lock. A project opened in the repository root
# leaves its lock beside the `.gpr`, not inside `*.rep/`, and that lock records
# the developer's hostname and username, hence the explicit pattern.
*.gpr
*.rep/
/OpenAntiGrav.lock*

# Emulator state
*.ppst
*.p2s
*.sav
*.state
*.state[0-9]

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agents. Local agent state stays out, but the checked-in Claude Code on the
# web setup does not: a re-included path cannot live under a wholly excluded
# directory, so the directory is globbed and the two tracked paths negated.
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
